// mecatl driver API: the remote skill-source protocol.
//
// SkillSourceService is the wire seam behind the harness's `tool.SkillSource`
// (engine/tool/skillsource.go): an operator-run driver process serves
// progressive-disclosure skills as LOGICAL BUNDLES — identity + trigger
// metadata (ListSkills), an instruction body (GetSkillBody), and auxiliary
// payloads addressed by LOGICAL name (ListSkillAssets/ReadSkillAsset). No
// path, directory, or root concept crosses this wire; where the driver keeps
// its bundles is its private business. The driver sits at the SAME trust tier
// as an operator-configured skills directory — a skill body steers the model
// like AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md, so point the harness only at a driver you trust.
//
// Driver contract (pinned by the engine/adapter/sourceconformance suite, which
// remote drivers run over their client):
//   - ListSkills returns the skill metadata sorted by name, unique, and STABLE
//     for the life of the source (snapshot semantics — the harness resolves
//     once at build; there is no watch/reload seam).
//   - GetSkillBody / ListSkillAssets of an unknown skill MUST return NOT_FOUND.
//   - ReadSkillAsset of an unknown skill OR asset MUST return NOT_FOUND.
//   - A logical asset name is slash-separated and RELATIVE: no leading
//     separator, no empty/"."/".." segments, no backslashes, no NUL. An
//     invalid name MUST be INVALID_ARGUMENT — never content (the harness-
//     provided Go server wrapper pre-validates via tool.ValidSkillAssetName).
//
// CAPACITY: ReadSkillAsset is unary and rides the protocol's 64 MiB required
// minimum message capacity (internal/adapter/grpcdriver.MaxSnapshotBytes; the
// harness additionally caps a single materialized asset at 16 MiB and a
// skill's whole bundle at 64 MiB).
//
// Validation: required-field annotations are authored with `buf.validate.field`
// for documentation and future runtime enforcement; V1 enforces them in the Go
// client/server wrappers (internal/adapter/grpcdriver).

